From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Chagas <drochachagas@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:59:11 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Shape tool: draw rectangles and ellipses as vector layers

A new toolbox tool, gimp-shape-tool (Photoshop's shape tools, U). Drag
on the canvas: a rectangle (optionally with rounded corners) or an
ellipse, Shift for a square or circle, Alt from the center. On release it
adds a path and a vector layer drawing it, in one undo step, with the fill
and stroke from the tool options (the Paths tool's vector layer editors;
filled with black and no stroke by default, as in Photoshop).

